    {
      "id": "txt_HX1caipp1yJoTT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1875.0,
      "y": 3180.0,
      "width": 761.6,
      "height": 25.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#5f3dc4",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9B",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 786675996,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 814379808,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792860000000,
      "created": 1792860000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why Unified ft_split() in parse_args() Handles All Argument Formats:",
      "fontSize": 20.0,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why Unified ft_split() in parse_args() Handles All Argument Formats:",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "txt_QyTxxhAeOsrQuv",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1875.0,
      "y": 3220.0,
      "width": 974.4000000000001,
      "height": 187.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9C",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 925841776,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 609627706,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792860000000,
      "created": 1792860000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Instead of branching on (argc == 2) vs (argc > 2), parse_args() runs ft_split(argv[i], ' ') on EVERY argv[i]:\n\n  1. Quoted multi-value string:   argv[1] = \"1 2 4 8\"  \u2500\u2500\u25ba ft_split produces 4 tokens: [\"1\", \"2\", \"4\", \"8\", NULL]\n  2. Single-value argument:       argv[2] = \"3\"        \u2500\u2500\u25ba ft_split produces 1 token:  [\"3\", NULL]\n  3. Mixed flags anywhere:        \"--bench 1 2\"        \u2500\u2500\u25ba process_tokens checks token[0..1] == \"--\" per token!\n\nDuplicate & Append Complexity for N = 8 Numbers:\n  \u2022 For the k-th inserted node, has_duplicate() traverses k existing nodes and append_node() traverses k-1 nodes.\n  \u2022 Total comparisons across ./push_swap \"1 2 4 8\" 3 5 6 7:  0 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 + 7 = 28 comparisons (O(N\u00b2)).\n  \u2022 Final check in parse_args(): if (!cfg->stack_a) exit_error(cfg); ensures at least 1 number was parsed.",
      "fontSize": 15.0,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Instead of branching on (argc == 2) vs (argc > 2), parse_args() runs ft_split(argv[i], ' ') on EVERY argv[i]:\n\n  1. Quoted multi-value string:   argv[1] = \"1 2 4 8\"  \u2500\u2500\u25ba ft_split produces 4 tokens: [\"1\", \"2\", \"4\", \"8\", NULL]\n  2. Single-value argument:       argv[2] = \"3\"        \u2500\u2500\u25ba ft_split produces 1 token:  [\"3\", NULL]\n  3. Mixed flags anywhere:        \"--bench 1 2\"        \u2500\u2500\u25ba process_tokens checks token[0..1] == \"--\" per token!\n\nDuplicate & Append Complexity for N = 8 Numbers:\n  \u2022 For the k-th inserted node, has_duplicate() traverses k existing nodes and append_node() traverses k-1 nodes.\n  \u2022 Total comparisons across ./push_swap \"1 2 4 8\" 3 5 6 7:  0 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 + 7 = 28 comparisons (O(N\u00b2)).\n  \u2022 Final check in parse_args(): if (!cfg->stack_a) exit_error(cfg); ensures at least 1 number was parsed.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
